+- Full-shard warnings observed: 38; shown warnings are existing PyTorch nested-tensor/Transformer warning classes, not V54 assertion failures.
+
+V54 science / provenance checks encoded in launcher
+---------------------------------------------------
+- exact V53 fit SHA256 lock:
+  9174ffeac064a85bef6c1727915d93903271f9afe1770f5e5ba3e3e51efe1b6e
+- exact V50.5 paired outcome SHA256 lock:
+  d592baa3508ae9dc084eebcbb3505d9accadc724601ab35a1253d3536af39d43
+- exact frozen population: 502 unique full-set RSMR proposal events;
+- treatment/control replan interval must match;
+- short replay uses the frozen replan interval as exposure window, no horizon sweep;
+- run_metric=false; no new full-horizon outcome labels;
+- exact target/probe identity checks inherited from frozen V50.5 runner;
+- synchronized iteration index and timestamp across treatment/control;
+- initial paired state must be identical;
+- physical-equality planned interventions must remain realized-equal within fail-closed tolerance;
+- planned scalar D in V54 profile must match V51/V52/V53 historical value token-by-token;
+- nested fit excludes outer test and calibration fold;
+- V54 writes a self-contained 502-row analysis population snapshot for future audit.
+
+Server-only validation boundary
+-------------------------------
+The current local environment does not contain the user's nuPlan package/raw DB/checkpoint, so the actual short-horizon two-arm simulation cannot be truthfully marked PASS here.
+The launcher therefore treats the first collision-safe 8-scene batch per arm as the fail-closed server sentinel. Any simulation/probe/trace mismatch stops before the remaining population is consumed.
